{title: I Am the Vine}
{subtitle: John 15:5}
{key: C}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | ×12

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I am the vine, you are the branches
Abide in me, and I in you
Who[F]ever abides in me bears much [C]fruit
For a[G]part from me you can do [C]nothing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Abide in me, abide in [Am]me
Abide [F]in my [G][C]love
Abide in me, abide in [Am]me
Abide in [F]my [G][C]love
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [C] | [C] | [Am] | [F] [G] | ×2
| [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
As the Father has loved me
[Am]So have I loved you
[F]By this my [G]Father is [C]glorified
That you [G]bear much [C]fruit
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Abide in me, abide in [Am]me
Abide in [F]my [G][C]love
Abide in me, abide in [Am]me
Abide in [F]my [G][C]love
{end_of_chorus}
